# Fixture for native_codegen.feature: proves bm_heap_init() now runs
# BEFORE main's own [BuildList, 0] "__globals" seed, so heap.patlang's
# own free-list table genuinely becomes the heap's first allocation for
# any program that uses Box -- found while measuring Phase 1 of docs/
# plans/general-refcounting.md: bm_heap_init used to run AFTER that seed,
# so bm_heap_fixed_ready() (the lock-free fast path check) could never be
# true for a real program with any other startup code, and every
# bm_alloc/bm_rc_inc/bm_rc_dec call fell through to the slow,
# "__vars"-lookup path instead (measured ~700x slower per alloc+drop
# cycle). A direct, deterministic check -- not a timing measurement,
# which would be flaky -- of bm_heap_fixed_ready() itself, right after
# the first box_new, is the correctness signal: true means the table
# landed at the heap's genuine first allocation.

let b = box_new(42)
# bm_heap_fixed_ready() itself can't be called here: box_new/box_get/
# box_share/box_set are each special, hardcoded keywords in
# bm_lower_program (their own dedicated IR opcodes, BoxNew/BoxGet/...),
# not ordinary declared-function calls -- so the lowerer has no notion
# of calling an arbitrary heap.patlang-internal name like this one, even
# though it's now correctly externed for LINKING (confirmed: heap_chunk
# .funcs was simply stale, missing every function issue #176's ticket
# lock added, including this one -- a real, separate, now-fixed bug,
# not a deliberate exclusion). Reproducing its exact two-line check with
# only already-recognized host-level primitives (mem_peek_qword,
# mem_heap_base) avoids needing a brand-new IR opcode just for this one
# assertion.
let is_fixed = mem_peek_qword(mem_heap_base(), 16) == 8102931470111
print("fixed_ready=" + is_fixed + " value=" + box_get(b))
